# MICROSLOP MASSACRE — quest definitions.
# === id | Title | main/side | xp | line
# stage-number  objective text @marker    (stage 100 or "done" = complete)
# Every objective says WHERE to go and HOW. Stage changes are driven by
# dialogue effects and by the story director (WorldObjects.TRIGGERS).
# Quest lines (+++ id | title): quests in a line are numbered in file order and
# hand the tracker to each other, so the next mission is always on screen.
+++ fsociety | fsociety
+++ darkarmy | The Dark Army
+++ fbi | The FBI
+++ ecorp | Tyrell Wellick
+++ les | The Lower East Side
+++ township | Washington Township
+++ bronx | The Bronx and Harlem
+++ odd | Odd Jobs
+++ lopez | The Detective
+++ wings | Bowery Bay
+++ respawn | Respawn
+++ rockstarved | Rockstarved Games
+++ chicago | The Windy City
+++ microslop | Microslop
+++ road | Out of Town

=== mq_hello | Hello, Friend | main | 150 | fsociety
Elliot Alderson. Cybersecurity engineer by day. By night, he reads people. Something was on his computer this morning that he doesn't remember putting there.
10 Go home: your building is two blocks east of Krista's, on the Lower East Side. Follow the marker @d_apt
20 Your computer has been running all day. Log in to your workstation in Apartment 4D @cell:elliot_apt:5.4,1.6
25 Gideon wants you at Allsafe in the morning. Tonight, do what Krista said: talk to the neighbors. Help at least two of them: the Super out front (no heat), Shayla in your hallway, Omar at the bodega (the corner crew) @npc:super
30 Morning. Allsafe Cybersecurity, Midtown. Gideon is waiting for you with the honeypot logs @npc:gideon
35 Pull the CS30 honeypot logs in Allsafe's server room and trace who knocked @cell:allsafe:17.4,4.2
40 done

=== mq_rootkit | The Coffee Shop | main | 250 | fsociety
The honeypot was hit from a coffee shop server on your own block. The same code as the file on your desktop. Gideon wants a name. You want to know who has been using your hands.
10 Go to Ron's Coffee, a few blocks west of your place. The server that touched E Corp is somewhere inside @d_ron
20 Find Ron's server in the back room and get in: hack it (HACKING) or get Ron to slip (SPEECH) @cell:ron_coffee:12,3
30 You know what Ron really sells. Confront him and decide what happens to him and his server @npc:ron
40 Plant the code from your desktop on Ron's server and see who answers (talk to Ron, or use the server) @cell:ron_coffee:12,3
50 An answer: 'Delancey Street station. Alone.' Go down to any subway platform @npc:robot_n
60 done

=== mq_fsociety | fsociety | main | 250 | fsociety
A man in an old field jacket knows your name, your habits, and the file on your desktop. He says you've met. You haven't. You'd remember. Wouldn't you?
10 Someone is waiting on the subway platform. Take any station's stairs down and find him @npc:robot_n
20 He said: Coney Island, the Fun Society Arcade, at the far south end of the city. The subway is fastest @d_arcade
30 Talk to the man in the jacket in the arcade's back room and hear what fsociety is building @npc:robot_n
40 done

=== mq_steel | Steel Mountain | main | 350 | fsociety
E Corp keeps its tape backups in a vault built into a hill upstate, with climate control, biometric doors and a manager who drinks alone. Encrypt the records without cooking the tapes, and E Corp restores everything by Christmas.
10 You need a way in and Mobley's device. Take the Raspberry Pi from the arcade stash. For a way in: buy Maintenance Coveralls at Ricky's, have Mobley forge a visitor badge, or get yourself a tour from Steel Mountain's manager, Bill Harper, who drinks at The Rabbit Hole @npc:bill_harper
20 You have what you need. Travel to Steel Mountain at the far north-east edge of the city. Wear the coveralls, carry the badge, or say Harper's name at the desk @d_steel
30 Get past security to the climate-control room at the back of the facility @cell:steel_mountain:20,6
40 Rig the climate control unit with the Raspberry Pi @cell:steel_mountain:20,6
50 done

=== mq_darkarmy | The Rose Garden | main | 350 | darkarmy
fsociety can't do this alone. In Chinatown there is an army that answers to one person, who keeps every clock in the world and never explains why. Armies have prices.
10 Make contact with the Dark Army: the Rose Garden Tea House in Chinatown. Ask for Cisco @d_rose
20 Cisco says Whiterose won't see you until Steel Mountain is done. Cook the mountain first @d_steel
30 Steel Mountain is ash. Whiterose will see you now, in the clock room at the back of the Rose Garden @npc:whiterose_n
35 Whiterose's price: when the FBI goes looking for fsociety's inside man, they must find Gideon Goddard. Do it at an Allsafe workstation, or build them a ghost instead, or warn Gideon and live with the consequences @cell:allsafe:11.5,4
40 done

=== mq_ecorp | The Inside Man | main | 350 | ecorp
The hack needs a door inside E Corp itself. Somebody opened Allsafe's honeypot from the inside, using Gideon's credentials. Somebody at E Corp wants to be standing next to the fire.
10 Get inside E Corp's headquarters in Midtown. Tyrell Wellick, SVP of Technology, has been asking about you in the lobby @npc:tyrell_n
20 Tyrell wants to talk properly. Meet him at his penthouse, the Wellick Residence @d_tyrell
30 Get to E Corp's network floor without Tyrell: take the keycard from the lobby security desk (or a guard), or wear an E Corp uniform, and ride the executive elevator @d_ecorp
40 You're on the network. Plug fsociety's femtocell (from the arcade stash) into the E Corp terminal on the 23rd floor @cell:ecorp_floor:13,3
50 done

=== mq_fbi | Person of Interest | main | 300 | fbi
Steel Mountain made the news. Now Special Agent Dominique DiPierro of the FBI's Cyber Division is in the city, and she has already said your name out loud.
10 Agent DiPierro wants a word. Federal Building, Lower Manhattan. Go before she comes to you @npc:dipierro
20 DiPierro wants an answer. Feed her the plan, refuse, offer her something bigger, or tell her everything @npc:dipierro
30 done

=== mq_respawn | Press Start | main | 250 | respawn
Darlene found a forum. Ten thousand people who paid for games E Corp switched off, accounts E Corp locked, studios E Corp bought and buried. They call themselves Respawn. They just need somebody to hand them a win.
10 Darlene's lead runs an invite-only board out of a shut-down game store. Meet Pixel at the arcade's back terminal @cell:arcade:17.6,4.5
20 Respawn wants proof the little guy can win. Pick E Corp's smallest, cruelest target first: Rockstarved Games, Floor 88 of the World Trade Center's North Tower, which E Corp quietly owns @d_wtc
30 done

=== mq_rs1 | Shark Bait | main | 300 | rockstarved
Rockstarved makes one great game a decade and sells pretend money for real money in between. 'Shark Cards.' A kid in Respawn spent his dead mother's savings on them. Get inside.
10 Rockstarved's floor is Floor 88 of the North Tower, up the WTC lobby's service elevator. You need a way up: lift a crunch-team badge off Kenny, the ex-QA tester who drinks at The Rabbit Hole, or talk him into giving you his @npc:kenny
20 Ride the WTC lobby elevator to Floor 88 and get onto the Rockstarved floor @d_wtc
30 Find Project Whale: the server that sorts every player by how much money can be squeezed out of them @cell:rockstarved_hq:1.6,10.7
40 done

=== mq_rs2 | Game Over, Man | main | 350 | rockstarved
You've seen how the sausage is made. Now break the machine and show the world the recipe: dump 'Project Whale' to every games site, crash the Shark Card store, or turn their own microtransactions against them.
10 You have Project Whale. Decide how Rockstarved falls: dump it to the press, crash the Shark Card servers from the floor terminal, or refund every whale at once @cell:rockstarved_hq:1.6,10.7
20 Respawn is louder than ever, and three more E Corp studios just got nervous. Tell Pixel it's working @cell:arcade:17.6,4.5
30 done

=== mq_chi1 | The Windy City | main | 300 | chicago
Electronic Arse and Phony both run their live-service empires out of Chicago, 790 miles west. Respawn has a cell there, in a dead warehouse on the South Side. Time to leave New York.
10 Get to Chicago: drive the interstate west out of the city, or fly there if you've got wings. It's a long way @region:chicago
20 Find the fsociety cell: a boarded warehouse on the Chicago South Side. Darlene set it up @d_chi_safe
30 done

=== mq_chi2 | Surprise Mechanics | main | 350 | chicago
Electronic Arse calls its loot boxes 'surprise mechanics' and sells them to kids. Their regional data center is in E Corp Midwest, downtown. Rig the next 'surprise' to surprise them.
10 Get into E Corp Midwest downtown (the blue tower in the Loop). Walk in by day, wear an E Corp uniform, or find another way @d_chi_node
20 Reach the data floor at the back and rig Electronic Arse's loot-box server so the odds are finally printed on the box @cell:chi_node:31,12
30 done

=== mq_chi3 | Account Suspended | main | 400 | chicago
Phony Interactive can revoke your library, your purchases, your account, any time, for any reason. So can you. Give every player their games back and lock Phony out of its own store.
10 Phony runs its account authority through the same Chicago data floor. Get back in and flip it: unlock every revoked library, and lock Phony's admins out of their own kingdom @cell:chi_node:31,12
20 Chicago's done, and every game company in the world just felt it. Head back to New York: I-90 east out of the South Side, or fly @region:nyc
30 done

=== mq_ms | Microslop Massacre | main | 600 | microslop
Microslop buys the studios people love and shuts them down. On Friday, on Floor 101 of the North Tower, it unveils Game Pass Away: every game ever made, rented back to you forever, and an AI that 'makes' the next ones. Respawn's last fight. The big one.
10 Pixel has a plan for Microslop. Take his call at the arcade's back terminal @cell:arcade:17.6,4.5
20 Microslop invited kennyQA to its showcase as a 'community voice.' Kenny's at The Rabbit Hole, and he's not going @npc:kenny
30 The showcase is on Floor 101 of the North Tower. Show Kenny's invitation at the WTC lobby's far-right elevator @d_wtc
40 Behind the stage is the Library: the license server for every studio Microslop ever bought. Find it in the back, or get its keeper, Brad Pitchley, to open it for you @cell:ms_floor:31,11
50 It's done. Tell Pixel. Tell everyone @cell:arcade:17.6,4.5
60 done

=== mq_robot | Who Is Mr. Robot | main | 400 | fsociety
Darlene looks at you like she's waiting for you to remember something. The man in the jacket finishes your sentences. The arcade's sign was painted over another sign. You are going to have to look.
10 Darlene wants you at her place, a few blocks from yours. She says it's important. She says it's been important for a long time @d_darlene
20 Look at the photograph Darlene keeps pinned above her desk @cell:darlene_apt:3,0.9
30 The old shop sign is still under the paint at the arcade. Look at it @cell:arcade:9,7.3
40 Mercy General Hospital keeps records going back to 1993. Find yours @cell:mercy_general:1.6,-2
50 He's waiting for you at the end of the Coney Island pier. It has to be night. It was always night @npc:robot_n
60 done

=== mq_finale | Five/Nine | main | 600 | fsociety
The biggest hack in history. To pull it off you need the mountain, an army, a door, and to have looked every player in this city in the eye: Whiterose, DiPierro, Tyrell. And yourself.
10 Five/Nine needs: Steel Mountain cooked, Whiterose and Agent DiPierro faced, a door into E Corp, and the truth about the man in the jacket. The plan board at the arcade lays it out @d_arcade
20 Everything is in place. Go back to the arcade and tell Mr. Robot to start the hack @npc:robot_n
30 It's done. The world woke up owing nothing. Now find out what that actually means @npc:darlene_n
40 An invitation: The Salina Hotel, Room 6. The people who really run things want a word @d_deus
50 done

=== mq_after | The Morning After | main | 400 | fsociety
The debt is gone. The ATMs are dark. And Phillip Price is already on television selling the cure: E Coin, E Corp's own money, in every pocket by Friday. You didn't burn the ledger. You handed him the next one.
10 Go home. Turn on the news. See what you did @cell:elliot_apt:3.4,3
20 Darlene called. She's called eleven times. Meet the crew at the arcade @npc:darlene_n
30 Stop Price from owning what comes next: poison the E Coin key batch at Consumer Credit branch 0419, take the story to the press, or hand Price to DiPierro @d_credit
40 done

=== sq_lou | Five Stars | side | 220 | road
Lou has sold red hots on the same South Side corner for thirty-one years. Three weeks ago he quit the EZeats delivery app over its 35% cut. The next morning, his rating fell from 4.8 to 1.2 overnight.
10 Lou keeps the reviews up on the tablet by his register, like a man pressing on a bruise. Read them @cell:chi_diner:8,1.4
20 Every one of the fake reviews was posted from the same address: the Skyway Motel, Room 14, on the South Side @d_chi_motel
30 Forty phones on a folding table, and a man named Trevor. Talk to him, or get into the review farm's laptop @cell:chi_motel:5,5.2
40 It's done, one way or another. Tell Lou @npc:lou
50 done

=== sq_rig | Last Load | side | 200 | road
Dolores has driven I-80 for twenty-two years. This morning her rig's autopilot subscription lapsed in a dead zone, and FreightOS locked the truck on the shoulder. In the trailer: insulin for the clinic in Lennox, with six hours of cold left.
10 Dolores is at the Big Rig Diner, out of options. Hear her out @npc:dolores
20 Her rig is locked on the west shoulder north of the diner. Jailbreak FreightOS, pull the telematics fuse, or take the insulin to Lennox yourself @poi_hw_rig
30 Get the insulin cooler to Ruth at the Lennox Pharmacy, south down I-80 past the motel, before it warms @npc:ruth
40 Let Dolores know how it went @npc:dolores
50 done

=== sq_ron | The Product | side | 120 | les
Ron doesn't sell coffee. He sells the ability to follow people who don't want to be followed. His customer list is a list of victims.
10 Find proof of what Ron really sells: his back-room server @cell:ron_coffee:12,3
20 Copy the customer database from the server @cell:ron_coffee:12,3
30 Confront Ron: report him, expose him, take the list, or walk away @npc:ron
50 done

=== sq_shayla | The Leverage | side | 300 | les
Shayla, your neighbor, owes money to Vera, who runs pills off the west side docks. Vera doesn't want the money. Vera wants the wizard next door.
10 Shayla owes Vera, and Vera's been asking about you. Keep an eye on her; she's usually in your building's hallway @npc:shayla_n
20 Shayla texted: Vera's crew grabbed her. Pier 9, west side docks. Find Dutch, Vera's man there: talk, pay, rob him, or take it off his body @npc:dutch
30 Vera's stash house, Coney Island, boardwalk side: the blue door. Case it first. Front door (if they'll let you talk), alley door round the back, or empty the house with Dutch's phone @pos:-137,520
35 Vera's price: erase 'People v. Vera' from the 7th Precinct's CaseTrack terminal, then go back to him @cell:precinct:14.5,-1.2
38 Vera's file is gone. Go back to the stash house; Vera has to keep his word @npc:vera
40 Get Shayla out of the cage in the back room. Pick the padlock or take the key off Dutch or the man with the shotgun @cell:vera_stash:11.5,-3.8
45 Shayla's out, and armed. Get her home to your building alive @d_apt
50 done

=== sq_krista | Small Disaster | side | 150 | les
Krista is seeing a man named Lenny. Lenny is lying to her about almost everything. You could tell her. You could ruin him. You could do both.
10 Krista's new boyfriend Lenny drinks at The Rabbit Hole. Look into him @npc:lenny
20 Get proof: sniff Lenny's phone off The Rabbit Hole's Wi-Fi router while he drinks, or crack it at his apartment (Lenny's Building, east side) @cell:rabbit_hole:11.6,0.8
30 You have proof. Confront Lenny at The Rabbit Hole, or go straight to Krista and decide what she gets to know @npc:krista
50 done

=== sq_colby | Washington Township | side | 200 | township
In 1993, a chemical leak in Washington Township killed people. Angela's mother. Elliot's father. E Corp buried it, and Terry Colby signed the shovel.
10 Somewhere in E Corp's records room is proof they knew. Find the Colby archive inside the E Corp tower @d_ecorp
20 You have the Colby emails. Bring them to Angela and decide what to do with the truth @npc:angela_n
50 done

=== sq_cat | Lost | side | 60 | odd
A woman by the park lost her dog. In this city, that's either nothing or everything.
10 Find Flipper the dog. Her owner says she loved the pier at Coney Island @cell:world:-30,840
20 Bring Flipper back to her owner @npc:catlady
50 done

=== sq_courier | Dead Drops | side | 100 | odd
The courier depot pays cash for no-questions deliveries. Some of the packages are fsociety's. Some are just packages.
10 Deliver the sealed package to the Gardener outside the Rose Garden Tea House in Chinatown @npc:gardener
20 Delivered. Go back to Dispatch for your money @npc:courier
50 done

=== sq_busker | Street Sermon | side | 80 | odd
A busker in the plaza has a mixtape she swears will change the world. She's not entirely wrong.
10 Get the busker's mixtape onto the pirate relay: the Relay Building roof, up in the Heights @d_relay
20 The signal's out. Go tell the busker @npc:busker
50 done

=== sq_bodega | Protection | side | 120 | les
Omar has run the bodega under your building for nineteen years. Lately Rico's corner crew has started collecting 'rent' at closing time. Omar has started closing early.
10 Rico's crew hangs on the corner a block west of your building after dark. Find Rico and end the shakedown: talk him off it, dig up leverage on his phone, buy Omar some peace, or put the crew down @npc:rico
20 Rico's crew is off Omar's corner. Tell Omar at the bodega @npc:omar
50 done

=== sq_super | No Heat | side | 80 | les
The building has no heat and the super has no plumber. You have a laptop and a grudge against E Corp's monopoly on boilers.
10 Fix the boiler controller at the back of your building's hallway @cell:apt_building:0.8,-12.5
20 Tell the Super the heat's back on @npc:super
50 done

=== sq_lopez | The Detective | side | 150 | lopez
The bodies you left behind have a pattern, and a homicide detective named Maria Lopez has started drawing it on a board.
10 A card under your door: 'Det. Maria Lopez, Homicide. Let's talk.' She works out of the 7th Precinct @npc:lopez
20 Lopez is building a case. Make it go away: wipe or rewrite her file on the precinct computer (the password is somewhere in the squad room), talk her down, pay her off, or deal with her @cell:precinct:14.5,-1.2
30 Lopez has enough to arrest you. She's waiting on the stairs of your building @npc:lopez
50 done

=== sq_candyman | Sugar | side | 300 | bronx
Somebody is selling 'candy' on the Carver Houses corners in the Bronx: bright little bags cut with something that stops kids' hearts. The whole block knows who. Nobody will say it out loud.
10 Mrs. Reyes buried her son last week. Find out who's selling the 'candy' on the Carver Houses corners. Start with the kid working the courtyard, Lil' Tee @npc:lil_tee
20 Candyman runs it from apartment 7C, Carver Houses Building C. Get inside (Tee can say your name to the door, or find your own way) and find out what he's cutting it with @npc:candyman
30 You know what Candyman is doing and where he cooks: Terminal Market Unit 9, Hunts Point. End it: take his ledger to Sgt. Brody at the 7th Precinct, burn the lab, turn his suppliers on him, make him retire, or take his corners @npc:candyman
40 It's over, one way or another. Go tell Mrs. Reyes at the candles in the Carver Houses courtyard @npc:mrs_reyes
50 done

=== sq_badco | Bad Company | side | 300 | bronx
A boy at a Harlem youth shelter has a new online friend who buys him things and tells him to keep secrets. The counselor who noticed can't get anyone to listen. You're very good at listening.
10 Ms. Okafor at the St. Nicholas Youth Shelter in Harlem is worried about Jaylen's online 'mentor'. Look at the phone he was given; it's on her office desk @cell:st_nicholas:20.6,1.1
20 The 'mentor' is Richard Keller, a youth soccer coach at 31-14 Ditmars Blvd, Astoria. Get in (men like him keep spare keys in the dumbest places) and get proof from his computer @d_keller
30 You have proof. Decide what happens to Richard Keller: take the drive to Sgt. Brody at the 7th Precinct or to Agent DiPierro, send it to the league's parents, squeeze him, or confront him yourself @npc:keller
40 It's done. Tell Ms. Okafor @npc:okafor
50 done

=== sq_wings | Wings | side | 250 | wings
Bowery Bay Airfield, Queens: one runway, three tired Skyhawks, and a man named Gus Petrakis who has thirty days before E Corp turns it all into a warehouse with a press release.
10 Find Gus Petrakis in the flight office at Bowery Bay Airfield, north of the Hunts Point subway @npc:gus
20 Take a Skyhawk from the apron and fly through Gus's five practice rings over the city @ring
30 Land the Skyhawk on the Bowery Bay runway and roll to a stop @pos:1570,-1280
40 You landed in one piece. Go see Gus in the flight office @npc:gus
50 E Corp Aviation Finance is foreclosing on the airfield. Talk to Gus and help him keep it, if you can @npc:gus
60 done
